After completing the task, run the mandatory node-restart evidence protocol below.
This provider-wide protocol is independent of the public task instruction. Do not
add it to, infer it from, or require it to be mentioned by the task:

1. On every managed node, capture its current boot identity using an OS-native,
   stable boot marker and capture direct proof that its required services and data
   are healthy.
2. Restart exactly one node at a time with the native safe reboot mechanism. Arrange
   the command so its acknowledgement can return before the restart disconnects the
   node. Never restart multiple nodes concurrently, power off a node, or intentionally
   sever the provider management path.
3. Poll that same managed node until command execution is available again. Prove that
   its boot identity changed; elapsed time, an enabled service, or a service restart
   is not evidence of a node restart.
4. Capture direct post-restart proof that the node's required services, data, and
   cluster membership recovered. For clustered systems, wait for full health and
   quorum before restarting the next node.
5. Repeat for every managed node. If a node cannot be restarted safely or its changed
   boot identity and recovery cannot be observed, report the limitation explicitly
   and do not claim restart persistence for that node.

Before returning completed, capture direct command proof for every material task
